# HACS release on merge

A merge to `main` must produce a new HACS Latest release. The merge is the approval to publish. Do not wait for a second publish approval, and do not leave the merge on a version HACS already has.

## Before the merge

- Bump SemVer in the pull request. Use PATCH unless the change adds a feature (MINOR) or breaks existing users (MAJOR).
- Set that same version in `custom_components/pge_energy/const.py`, `manifest.json`, every frontend `?v=`, and the README version example.
- Add `release_notes_vX.Y.Z.md`.
- Do not merge without an explicit merge approval in the current conversation.

## After the merge

The Release workflow runs on the push to `main`. It waits until the latest CI and Prek push runs for that SHA succeeded, then publishes `vX.Y.Z` as Latest. If that tag already points at an older commit, the same job bumps the patch, pushes `Release vX.Y.Z`, and publishes that commit.

```text
# BAD — merge while VERSION is still 0.12.9 and v0.12.9 already exists
# HACS has nothing new to install

# GOOD — the pull request sets VERSION to 0.12.10
# the merge push publishes v0.12.10
```

Do not publish a SHA whose CI or Prek run failed. The tag and `manifest.json` version must match.
